section: identity
title: Identity and permissions
about: |
  The cloud account of the cluster, the role or the key behind it, and the permissions the build
  needs of it. Palette checks that a role can be assumed and that policies exist, not that the role
  can build the cluster type.
rules:
- id: eks-role-no-eks-policy
  title: The role of the cloud account holds the EKS policy
  engines:
  - eks
  tier: cloud
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  when: .account.spec.credentialType == "sts"
  what: |
    An STS role without the EKS policy of Palette fails with `AccessDenied` on `eks:DescribeCluster`
    at create, after a full apply. The EKS name check of Palette finds it by chance; a role that can
    describe but not create passes it. `POST /v1/clouds/eks/properties/validate` is that name check.
    The check simulates the EKS and IAM actions of the build against the resources the build
    names. Those are the cluster ARN and a node group ARN of the cluster name, and the three CAPA
    roles. The EKS policy of Palette scopes `eks:CreateCluster` and `eks:DescribeCluster` to
    `arn:*:eks:*:*:cluster/*`. So a simulation with no `--resource-arns` answers `implicitDeny`
    for a role that builds clusters. An action counts as allowed when one listed resource allows
    it. The simulator has no request context. So an `implicitDeny` on an action that a condition
    key allows is a warning to read, not a proof. The role that built the #89 clusters gets
    `implicitDeny` on `eks:CreateCluster` against every resource. `role-partial-permissions`
    simulates the resource-less EC2 actions of the same policies.
  check:
    kind: exec
    needs:
    - aws
    argv:
    - aws
    - iam
    - simulate-principal-policy
    - --policy-source-arn
    - '{{ .account.spec.sts.arn }}'
    - --action-names
    - eks:CreateCluster
    - eks:CreateNodegroup
    - eks:DescribeCluster
    - eks:DescribeNodegroup
    - iam:PassRole
    - iam:GetRole
    - iam:ListAttachedRolePolicies
    - --resource-arns
    - arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:eks:{{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }}:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:cluster/{{ .entity.metadata.name }}
    - arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:eks:{{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }}:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:nodegroup/{{ .entity.metadata.name }}/{{ [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | select((.poolConfig.isControlPlane // false) | not) | .poolConfig.name ] | .[0] // "worker-pool" }}/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
    - arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}control-plane.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io
    - arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}nodes.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io
    - arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}controllers.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io
    - --output
    - json
    expr: |
      def allowed: .EvalDecision == "allowed" or any((.ResourceSpecificResults // [])[]; .EvalResourceDecision == "allowed");
      def per_resource: [ (.ResourceSpecificResults // [])[] | "\(.EvalResourceName | split(":") | .[5:] | join(":")) \(.EvalResourceDecision)" ] | join(", ");
      if .exec.exit != 0 then ["aws iam simulate-principal-policy failed: \(.exec.stderr | tostring | .[:200])"]
      else [ (.exec.stdout.EvaluationResults // [])[] | select(allowed | not)
             | "\(.EvalActionName) is \(.EvalDecision) for the role on each resource of the build (\(per_resource)); the simulator has no request context, so read this as a warning: the role of #89 builds clusters and gets implicitDeny on eks:CreateCluster" ] end
  reproduce:
  - aws iam simulate-principal-policy --policy-source-arn {{ .account.spec.sts.arn }} --action-names eks:CreateCluster eks:CreateNodegroup eks:DescribeCluster iam:PassRole --resource-arns arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:eks:{{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }}:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:cluster/{{ .entity.metadata.name }} arn:{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[1] }}:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}nodes.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io --query 'EvaluationResults[].[EvalActionName,EvalDecision,ResourceSpecificResults[].EvalResourceDecision]' --output json
  - 'aws iam list-attached-role-policies --role-name {{ (.account.spec.sts.arn // "") | split("/") | .[-1] }} --query ''AttachedPolicies[].PolicyName'' --output text   # the EKS policy of Palette must be among them'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: A permission check for each cloud type (SimulatePrincipalPolicy) in the validate route.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#89'
  - kind: run
    ref: preflight-plan eks 20260929T042910Z
    note: the simulation with no --resource-arns gave implicitDeny for eks:CreateNodegroup and eks:DescribeCluster on the role that built the
  - kind: source
    ref: docs/src/development/live-example.md
    note: the EKS policy of Palette that the live example attaches to its role gives eks:CreateCluster, eks:DescribeCluster, and eks:ListClusters on arn:*:eks:*:*:cluster/* and arn:*:eks:*:*:nodegroup/*/*/*
  - kind: report
    ref: palette-precreate-validation-gaps-findings-2026-09-28 F4
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/public-cloud/aws/required-iam-policies/additional-iam-policies-specific-use-cases/
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/role-denied.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/role-allowed.json
- id: role-partial-permissions
  title: The role of the cloud account can call each action of the build
  engines:
  - aws
  - eks
  tier: cloud
  severity: warn
  status: source
  when: .account.spec.credentialType == "sts"
  what: |
    Palette checks that the role can be assumed and that its policy ARNs exist. It does not check
    that the role can build the cluster type. A role that can call `DescribeCluster` and not
    `CreateCluster`, `CreateNodegroup`, or `iam:PassRole` passes each Palette check and fails
    during the build. The check simulates the 13 EC2, load balancer, and CloudFormation actions
    of the documented policies. The policies grant them on the resource `*`. The check counts the
    ones this build calls: a static network (`vpcId` set) drops the VPC actions, EKS drops the
    instance actions, and a manual CloudFormation stack drops `cloudformation:DescribeStacks`.
    The EKS and IAM actions are scoped to a cluster, a node group, or a role. A simulation with no
    `--resource-arns` answers `implicitDeny` for them on a role that builds clusters.
    `eks-role-no-eks-policy` simulates them against the ARNs of the build. The second reproduce
    line simulates `iam:PassRole` against the three CAPA roles. The simulator has no request
    context. So an `implicitDeny` on an action that a condition key allows is a warning to read,
    not a proof. A `secret` account has no ARN in the world, and the rule skips it.
  check:
    kind: exec
    needs:
    - aws
    argv:
    - aws
    - iam
    - simulate-principal-policy
    - --policy-source-arn
    - '{{ .account.spec.sts.arn }}'
    - --action-names
    - ec2:CreateSecurityGroup
    - ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress
    - ec2:DescribeKeyPairs
    - ec2:DescribeImages
    - ec2:RunInstances
    - elasticloadbalancing:CreateLoadBalancer
    - ec2:CreateVpc
    - ec2:CreateSubnet
    - ec2:CreateInternetGateway
    - ec2:CreateRouteTable
    - ec2:CreateNatGateway
    - ec2:AllocateAddress
    - cloudformation:DescribeStacks
    - --output
    - json
    expr: |
      def always: ["ec2:CreateSecurityGroup", "ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress"];
      def aws_only: ["ec2:DescribeImages", "ec2:RunInstances", "elasticloadbalancing:CreateLoadBalancer"];
      def dynamic: ["ec2:CreateVpc", "ec2:CreateSubnet", "ec2:CreateInternetGateway", "ec2:CreateRouteTable", "ec2:CreateNatGateway", "ec2:AllocateAddress"];
      def manual: [ (.profiles // [])[] | .packs[] | select(.layer == "k8s") | (.valuesCanon.manageCloudFormationStackManually.enabled // false) ] | any;
      ( always
        + (if .cloud == "eks" then [] else aws_only end)
        + (if (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.vpcId // "") == "" then dynamic else [] end)
        + (if (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.sshKeyName // "") != "" then ["ec2:DescribeKeyPairs"] else [] end)
        + (if manual then [] else ["cloudformation:DescribeStacks"] end) ) as $need
      | if .exec.exit != 0 then ["aws iam simulate-principal-policy failed: \(.exec.stderr | tostring | .[:200])"]
        else [ (.exec.stdout.EvaluationResults // [])[]
               | select(.EvalDecision != "allowed")
               | select(.EvalActionName as $a | ($need | index($a)) != null)
               | "\(.EvalActionName) is \(.EvalDecision) for the role on the resource *, and this build calls it; the simulator has no request context, so read this as a warning" ] end
  reproduce:
  - aws iam simulate-principal-policy --policy-source-arn {{ .account.spec.sts.arn }} --action-names ec2:RunInstances ec2:CreateVpc ec2:CreateSecurityGroup ec2:CreateNatGateway cloudformation:DescribeStacks --query 'EvaluationResults[].[EvalActionName,EvalDecision]' --output table
  - aws iam simulate-principal-policy --policy-source-arn {{ .account.spec.sts.arn }} --action-names iam:PassRole --resource-arns arn:aws:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}control-plane.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io arn:aws:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}nodes.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io arn:aws:iam::{{ .account.spec.sts.arn | split(":") | .[4] }}:role/{{ .account.spec.namePrefix // "" }}controllers.cluster-api-provider-aws.sigs.k8s.io --query 'EvaluationResults[].[EvalActionName,EvalResourceName,EvalDecision]' --output table
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: A permission check for each cloud type (SimulatePrincipalPolicy) in the validate route, with the actions of the documented policies and the resources of the build.
  evidence:
  - kind: report
    ref: palette-precreate-validation-gaps-findings-2026-09-28 B5
  - kind: run
    ref: preflight-plan aws 20260929T041905Z, eks 20260929T042910Z
    note: with no --resource-arns, iam:PassRole and the EKS actions gave implicitDeny on roles that build clusters; the EC2, load balancer, and CloudFormation actions gave allowed
  - kind: source
    note: the account validate of Palette assumes the role and calls DescribeRegions; it calls GetPolicy on each policy ARN
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/public-cloud/aws/required-iam-policies/
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/role-partial.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/identity-clean.json
- id: sts-account-not-assumable
  title: The STS cloud account can be assumed
  engines:
  - aws
  - eks
  tier: palette
  severity: fail
  status: seen
  when: .account.spec.credentialType == "sts"
  what: |
    Palette creates an STS cloud account over a role that does not exist, or that its trust
    policy refuses. The cluster then fails with `AwsKeyPairsReadError` or an AssumeRole 403.
    `POST /v1/clouds/aws/account/validate` answers in seconds, and a cluster create does not call
    it.
  check:
    kind: palette
    method: POST
    path: /v1/clouds/aws/account/validate
    body: .account.spec
    expr: |
      if .response.ok then [] else ["Palette cannot use the account \(.account.metadata.name // .entity.spec.cloudAccountUid): \(.response.body.code // .response.status): \(.response.body.message // "")"] end
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Run the account check at cluster create.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: teardown lab
  - kind: source
    note: assumes the role with the external id, then calls DescribeRegions
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/account-refused.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/clean.json
